# Wave W17-U (Route 204): bluff turf — bluff-foot turf with scree flecks: a bright foot-of-the-bluff green carrying pale and mid-grey stone flecks fallen off the slope above (design: the cave under the north bluff; the shipped flowerfield banks and honeytree stand byte-preserved by spec as the route’s biome dressing, and the ground converts around them). Route 204’s own ground — split from Route 203’s smoke-greyed coal turf by the scree (fallen stone vs blown dust) and from Route 201’s shore meadow by register (bluff foot vs lake shore).
